TOTK: an Ampere formatted surface load or store (SULD.P, SUST.P) of an image the host says is viewed with an integer format
(IGpuAccessor.QueryAnsweredImageFormat, Program.cs: the job's "img" fmt) declares the image with that format, so the registers
are read and written as raw bits, as the hardware does through such a view. Ryujinx leaves a formatted access's image
without a format when the host loads formatted images, which makes it float: OoT's forest cutscene writes
shared-exponent colour words through an NVN R32UI view of an R11G11B10F texture (a335c1db6270c355), and as floats they were
converted into red, clamped and NaN values. Without an answer, or with a float one, nothing changes; Maxwell jobs are
unchanged.

